          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              Assuming impredicative foundations, there is an archimedean field
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              which is Dedekind-complete, and into which every archimedean field embeds. Furthermore, every Dedekind-complete ordered field is isomorphic to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Construct
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              using, say, Dedekind cuts of rational numbers. Then it is well known how to prove these facts about
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
          %p
            However, we note that the proof is valid in weak
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foundations"} foundations
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            with a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers+object"} natural numbers object
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers+object"} real numbers object
          %p
            Even weaker foundations are possible if one allows the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying+set"} underlying set
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            to be
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+class"} large
          %p
            However, if we are working in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicative+mathematics"} predicative mathematics
            with multiple
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universes"} universes
            in the foundation, the Dedekind real numbers would no longer be unique up to unique isomorphism, but rather there would be a set of Dedekind real numbers for each universe.
          %h3#the_cauchy_complete_ordered_field The Cauchy complete ordered field
